Makes the simulated host serve fetches by version again, as before 5c20f3d
(§7.5 steps 2 and 3): a source serves the file at the requested path only if
its live record there is exactly the wanted version, and no longer serves the
wanted content from a record of another version or from another path. A
conflict's merged version M exists nowhere until someone merges, so the
winner's holders, which hold M's content under an older version, answer
NotAvailable for it again. The request by hash lives in the host (the engine's
Fetch action already carries the version, for its report), so this is the
smallest place to turn it off; the engine half of 5c20f3d, which keys a
want's sources by content, is left as it is.

test: delocal-sim regressions::content_is_fetched_by_hash_from_whoever_holds_it
test: delocal-sim sim::tests::a_source_serves_the_wanted_content_under_any_version_or_path

